msgid "Command mode with Aesh"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/aeshell/aesh[Aesh] is a Java library for building "
"interactive command line applications.\n"
"It supports option parsing, tab completion, command grouping, and an "
"interactive shell (REPL) mode.\n"
"For more details about the Aesh library itself, see the https://aeshell."
"github.io/[Aesh documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides support for using Aesh. This guide contains examples of the "
"`aesh` extension usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once you have your Quarkus project configured you can add the `aesh` "
"extension\n"
"to your project by running the following command in your project base "
"directory."
msgstr ""

msgid "This will add the following to your build file:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For optimal performance (especially in native mode), add the Aesh annotation "
"processor to\n"
"your Maven compiler plugin configuration. This generates compile-time "
"command metadata,\n"
"eliminating reflection-based annotation scanning at runtime:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The annotation processor is optional. Without it, Aesh falls back to runtime\n"
"reflection for command metadata, which works correctly but is slower at "
"startup."
msgstr ""

msgid "Building a command line application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Aesh extension supports two execution modes, controlled by the `quarkus."
"aesh.mode` build-time property.\n"
"Console mode is what makes Aesh distinctive -- it provides an interactive "
"shell (REPL) where users can type multiple commands with tab completion and "
"command history.\n"
"Runtime mode executes a single command and exits, like a standard CLI tool.\n"
"In most cases, the mode is auto-detected based on your command annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Console mode (interactive shell)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Console mode starts an interactive shell (REPL) where users can type "
"multiple commands.\n"
"This is what differentiates Aesh from other CLI frameworks: users get an "
"interactive session\n"
"with tab completion, command history, and shared state across commands."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Console mode is automatically selected when there are multiple "
"`@CommandDefinition` classes\n"
"without `groupCommands`, when there are multiple independent commands,\n"
"or when a remote transport (WebSocket or SSH) is present.\n"
"You can also force it with `quarkus.aesh.mode=console`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With two commands, console mode is auto-detected. Without arguments, the "
"interactive\n"
"REPL starts:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If command-line arguments are provided, the command is executed once and the "
"application\n"
"exits -- just like runtime mode:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This allows console mode applications to be used both interactively and in "
"scripts."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The prompt, exit command, and other console settings are configurable via "
"`quarkus.aesh.*` properties."
msgstr ""

msgid "Group commands in console mode (sub-command mode)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use `@CommandDefinition` with `groupCommands` in console mode to "
"create command groups with sub-command mode.\n"
"When a user types a group command without a sub-command, they enter an "
"interactive context for that group:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sub-commands listed in `groupCommands` are only accessible through their "
"parent group -- they do not appear as top-level commands in the shell."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Sub-commands use `@CommandDefinition` without `groupCommands`. The extension "
"automatically excludes them from top-level registration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CDI injection works in sub-commands. The extension injects `@Inject` fields "
"after Aesh creates the sub-command instances."
msgstr ""

msgid "An interactive session using sub-command mode:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sub-commands can be called directly with their parent prefix."
msgstr ""

msgid "Typing just the group command name enters sub-command mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Inside sub-command mode, type sub-commands directly without the parent "
"prefix."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Type `exit` (or `..`) to leave sub-command mode and return to the main "
"prompt."
msgstr ""

msgid "Runtime mode (single command execution)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is the default mode when there is a single `@CommandDefinition` or a "
"`@CommandDefinition` with `groupCommands`.\n"
"The application executes one command and exits, similar to standard CLI "
"tools."
msgstr ""

msgid "Simple application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A simple Aesh application with a single command can be created as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If there is only one class annotated with `@CommandDefinition`, it is "
"automatically used as the entry point of the command line application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All command classes are registered as CDI beans. You can use `@Inject` to "
"inject other beans."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Beans annotated with `@CommandDefinition` should not use proxied scopes (e.g."
" do not use `@ApplicationScoped`)\n"
"because Aesh sets field values directly via reflection.\n"
"By default, the Aesh extension registers command classes with the "
"`@Dependent` scope."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grouped commands with subcommands"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`groupCommands` lists the subcommands available under this parent command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@ParentCommand` injects the parent command, giving access to parent options "
"like `--verbose`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The application can then be invoked as:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Programmatic sub-commands with GroupCommand"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead of declaring sub-commands in the `groupCommands` annotation "
"attribute, you can implement the `GroupCommand` interface and override "
"`getCommands()` to register sub-commands programmatically.\n"
"This is useful when sub-commands need constructor arguments or when the set "
"of sub-commands is determined at runtime:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implement `GroupCommand` instead of plain `Command`. Do not use "
"`groupCommands` in the annotation -- the sub-commands come from "
"`getCommands()` instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Inject the sub-command via CDI so that `@Inject` fields in the sub-command "
"are properly populated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Return CDI-managed instances from `getCommands()`. Aesh uses these instances "
"directly, preserving CDI injection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CDI injection works in sub-commands because they are managed by CDI, not "
"created with `new`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom option completers, converters, and validators"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Aesh supports custom implementations for tab-completion, type conversion, "
"option validation, and more.\n"
"These implementations are CDI beans, so they can inject services:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reference custom completers, validators, and converters via their class in "
"annotation attributes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CDI beans implementing aesh interfaces (`OptionCompleter`, "
"`OptionValidator`, `Converter`, `CommandActivator`, etc.) are automatically "
"kept by Arc even though they are only referenced from annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Completers can inject CDI services. This is particularly useful in console "
"mode, where a completer can offer context-aware suggestions based on "
"application state (e.g., completing task names from a service)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mixins (reusable option groups)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mixins allow you to define a set of options in a separate class and reuse "
"them across multiple commands.\n"
"Use the `@Mixin` annotation to include a mixin's options in a command:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The mixin class is a plain Java class with `@Option` fields. It does not "
"need any annotations on the class itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Commands include the mixin with `@Mixin`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The mixin's options (`--format`, `--verbose`) are added to the command as if "
"they were declared directly on it. Tab completion and help output include "
"them automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dynamic default values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can provide dynamic default values for command options by implementing "
"the `DefaultValueProvider` interface as a CDI bean.\n"
"The extension automatically discovers and applies it to all commands:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Register as a CDI bean. The extension discovers it automatically -- no "
"additional wiring needed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Return `null` to use the annotation-declared default. Return a value to "
"override it at runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Per-command providers can also be specified via "
"`@CommandDefinition(defaultValueProvider = MyProvider.class)`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Option features"
msgstr ""

msgid "Allowed values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Restrict an option to a fixed set of values with `allowedValues`. Invalid "
"values are rejected at parse time,\n"
"and tab completion automatically suggests the allowed values:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fallback values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `fallbackValue` for three-state options where the option can be omitted, "
"specified without a value,\n"
"or specified with an explicit value:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`--debug` alone uses the fallback value `\"5005\"`. `--debug=8000` uses the "
"explicit value. Omitting the option entirely uses the `defaultValue` (if "
"set)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Customizing CLI settings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can customize the underlying Aesh `SettingsBuilder` by implementing the "
"`CliSettings` interface:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Multiple `CliSettings` beans can be registered. They are applied in "
"arbitrary order, so avoid conflicting settings across implementations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom CommandInvocation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use `CliSettings` to register a custom `CommandInvocationProvider` "
"that wraps the default `CommandInvocation` with application-specific context."
"\n"
"This is useful when commands need shared state or services that are not "
"available through CDI injection:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Commands can then declare the custom invocation type and access the "
"additional context:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The custom `CommandInvocationProvider` is applied in all execution modes: "
"console REPL, console single-command execution (with arguments), and runtime "
"mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Similarly, you can register custom `ConverterInvocationProvider` and "
"`ValidatorInvocationProvider` implementations to pass additional context to "
"converters and validators."
msgstr ""

msgid "Command execution listener"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implement `CommandExecutionListener` as a CDI bean to receive a callback "
"after each command completes.\n"
"This is useful for logging, metrics, or audit trails:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The listener fires in both console mode (after each REPL command) and when "
"arguments are provided on the command line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Command not found handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implement `CommandNotFoundHandler` as a CDI bean to customize the error "
"message when an unknown command is typed:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Build-time validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Aesh extension validates command configurations at build time. Invalid "
"configurations are reported as deployment failures with descriptive error "
"messages, so you can fix them before the application starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "The following checks are performed:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Duplicate top-level command names** -- two or more top-level command "
"classes with the same `@CommandDefinition(name = \"...\")` value."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Missing `@CommandDefinition` on group sub-commands** -- a class listed in "
"`@CommandDefinition(groupCommands = {...})` that is not annotated with "
"`@CommandDefinition`.\n"
"*"
msgstr ""

msgid "Remote terminal access"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Aesh extension provides optional sub-extensions for remote terminal "
"access via WebSocket and SSH.\n"
"These allow users to interact with your CLI application from a browser or an "
"SSH client while the application is running in console mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "WebSocket terminal"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the `quarkus-aesh-websocket` dependency to expose a browser-based "
"terminal:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Once added, the terminal is accessible at `http://localhost:8080/aesh/index."
"html` when the application is running."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The built-in terminal page uses https://xtermjs.org/[xterm.js], which is "
"bundled with the extension.\n"
"No external CDN or internet access is required."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The WebSocket endpoint is registered at `/aesh/terminal` by default. You can "
"change the endpoint path:"
msgstr ""

msgid "To disable the WebSocket endpoint:"
msgstr ""

msgid "WebSocket authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The WebSocket terminal endpoint has no authentication by default. You can "
"secure it by\n"
"requiring an authenticated user or restricting access to specific roles. "
"Both options\n"
"require a Quarkus Security extension to be present (e.g., `quarkus-elytron-"
"security-properties-file`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "To require any authenticated user:"
msgstr ""

msgid "To restrict access to specific roles:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When `roles-allowed` is set, `authenticated` is ignored since role-based "
"access implies authentication."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension will log a warning at build time if the WebSocket terminal is "
"enabled\n"
"in production without authentication configured."
msgstr ""

msgid "SSH terminal"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the `quarkus-aesh-ssh` dependency to expose an SSH server:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Connect to the terminal with any SSH client:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Password and public key authentication can be used simultaneously. When both "
"are configured,\n"
"clients can authenticate with either method. If neither is configured, any "
"password is accepted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension will log a warning at startup if the SSH server is running "
"without\n"
"any authentication configured (no password, no authorized-keys-file)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connection management"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both SSH and WebSocket transports support limiting concurrent sessions and "
"closing idle connections."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When `max-connections` is set, new connections beyond the limit are rejected "
"immediately. When `idle-timeout` is set, sessions with no input activity for "
"the specified duration are closed automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Session events"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension fires CDI events when remote sessions open and close. Use "
"these to monitor session lifecycle, log access, or perform cleanup:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Events are fired asynchronously. Use `@ObservesAsync` (not `@Observes`) to "
"receive them."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `AeshSessionEvent` payload provides:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`sessionId()` -- unique identifier for the session"
msgstr ""

msgid "`transport()` -- `\"ssh\"` or `\"websocket\"`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`timestamp()` -- when the event occurred"
msgstr ""

msgid "Events are fired for both SSH and WebSocket sessions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Health checks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `quarkus-smallrye-health` extension is present, readiness health "
"checks are automatically registered for SSH and WebSocket transports. The "
"health endpoints report whether each transport is running and the number of "
"active connections."
msgstr ""

msgid "To disable the health checks:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Local console behavior with remote transports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a remote transport extension (`quarkus-aesh-websocket` or `quarkus-aesh-"
"ssh`) is present,\n"
"the local console (stdin/stdout) is **not started by default**. This means "
"the application starts\n"
"as a normal Quarkus server, and CLI access is available only through the "
"remote transport."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This auto-detection prevents the local console from blocking the terminal "
"when the application\n"
"is intended to run as a server with remote CLI access."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can override this behavior with the `quarkus.aesh.start-console` "
"property:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The auto-detection logic:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No remote transport present -> local console **starts** (default CLI "
"application behavior)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Remote transport present -> local console **skipped** (server mode with "
"remote CLI access)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.aesh.start-console` explicitly set -> overrides auto-detection in "
"either direction"
msgstr ""

msgid "Security considerations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**SSH**: Use `quarkus.aesh.ssh.authorized-keys-file` for public key "
"authentication (recommended),\n"
"or set `quarkus.aesh.ssh.password` for password authentication (use "
"`${SSH_PASSWORD}` to avoid\n"
"storing the password in plaintext). Both methods can be used simultaneously.\n"
"Without either, any password is accepted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**WebSocket**: Set `quarkus.aesh.websocket.authenticated=true` or `quarkus."
"aesh.websocket.roles-allowed`\n"
"to require authentication. This requires a Quarkus Security extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additionally, restrict network access to these endpoints using firewalls or "
"bind addresses.\n"
"Use `idle-timeout` to automatically close abandoned sessions and `max-"
"connections` to limit concurrent sessions and prevent resource exhaustion. "
"Health checks (when `quarkus-smallrye-health` is present) provide visibility "
"into the number of active sessions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"WebSocket connections are not protected by the browser's same-origin policy.\n"
"If the WebSocket terminal is exposed on a network, consider configuring CORS "
"via the\n"
"`quarkus.http.cors` settings to restrict which origins can connect."
msgstr ""

msgid "Providing your own QuarkusMain"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also provide your own application entry point annotated with "
"`@QuarkusMain` (as described in xref:command-mode-reference.adoc[Command "
"Mode reference guide]).\n"
"When a `@QuarkusMain` is present, the Aesh extension will not register its "
"own runner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Development Mode"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In development mode (`mvn quarkus:dev`), the Quarkus dev console takes "
"control of the terminal for its interactive features (live reload, test "
"output, etc.).\n"
"This means the local terminal is not available for aesh CLI interaction."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To test your CLI commands during development, you have the following options:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**WebSocket terminal**: Add the `quarkus-aesh-websocket` dependency and "
"access the CLI via browser at `http://localhost:8080/aesh/index.html`. The "
"dev console stays on the local terminal while the aesh CLI runs in the "
"browser."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Pass arguments**: Use `mvn quarkus:dev -Dquarkus.args='--help'` or `mvn "
"quarkus:dev -Dquarkus.args='-n Quarkus'` to pass arguments directly. The "
"application is re-executed every time the `Space bar` key is pressed. For "
"Gradle projects, use `--quarkus-args`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Build and run**: Build the application with `mvn package -DskipTests` and "
"run it directly with `java -jar target/quarkus-app/quarkus-run.jar <command> "
"[options]`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Aesh extension provides Dev UI pages accessible at `http://localhost:"
"8080/q/dev-ui` when running in development mode. The Aesh card in the Dev UI "
"offers up to three pages depending on which sub-extensions are present."
msgstr ""

msgid "Commands page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Always available. Shows a table of all discovered CLI commands with their "
"name, description, type (Group or regular), class name, and sub-commands for "
"group commands. The resolved execution mode (console or runtime) is "
"displayed at the top. A search field allows filtering commands by name, "
"description, or class name."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sessions page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Available when a remote transport extension (`quarkus-aesh-websocket` or "
"`quarkus-aesh-ssh`) is present. Displays transport cards showing the status, "
"active session count, and maximum session limit for each transport. Below "
"the cards, a live event log shows session opened and closed events in real-"
"time as users connect and disconnect."
msgstr ""

msgid "Terminal page"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Available when the `quarkus-aesh-websocket` extension is present. Embeds an "
"interactive terminal directly in the Dev UI using https://xtermjs.org/[xterm."
"js]. Click **Connect** to open a WebSocket connection to the terminal "
"endpoint and interact with your CLI commands from the browser. The terminal "
"supports the same features as the standalone terminal page (color, resize, "
"unicode)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Aesh commands can be tested with `@QuarkusMainTest` from the xref:command-"
"mode-reference.adoc[Command Mode reference guide].\n"
"The approach differs depending on the execution mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing runtime mode commands"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Runtime mode commands execute once and exit.\n"
"Use `@Launch` to run them with specific arguments and assert on the output:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing console mode commands (REPL)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Console mode commands run in an interactive shell.\n"
"Use `AeshLauncher` to start a REPL session, send commands, and assert on "
"their output:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`AeshLauncher` provides:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`launch(String... args)` -- starts the REPL on a background thread"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`executeCommand(String command)` -- sends a command and blocks until it "
"completes (10 second default timeout)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`executeCommand(String command, Duration timeout)` -- same with a custom "
"timeout"
msgstr ""

msgid "`getErrorOutput()` -- returns any error output from the session"
msgstr ""

msgid "`exit()` -- sends the exit command and waits for clean shutdown"
msgstr ""

msgid "Packaging your application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An Aesh command line application is a standard Quarkus application and can "
"be packaged as a JAR or a native executable."
msgstr ""

msgid "As a jar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Building an uber-jar is practical if you plan on distributing the JAR "
"directly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "As a native executable"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can build a https://quarkus.io/guides/building-native-image[native "
"executable] for faster startup and lower memory usage:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Aesh extension automatically registers command classes and their option "
"types for reflection in native builds."
msgstr ""

